#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064012 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60a223c7-3d1c-50d6-be7c-330ba039635c" :question/math-academy-id "e-491" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle  \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle  \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{7x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}-\\int \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}\\int {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{{e}^{7x}}{7})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{49}{e}^{7x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064013 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "804f45cd-2082-5521-b4db-a32169716626" :question/math-academy-id "e-492" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x \\cos{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int vu'\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x \\cos{2x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064030 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aaeb0407-771b-5dbc-8a50-e7bc0e3477c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-6209" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/5} x\\sin(5x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+{\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)]+[\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\cdot (-1)+0]+[0-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289105 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7558fff-d697-5dda-879e-5b66e4da6fe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x{e}^{-3x}+\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289107} {:answer/id #uuid "0337ec50-1281-5f53-87d6-01d2705a10f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289108} {:answer/id #uuid "bddc3cf2-3f22-5caf-93ac-23307c7115ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289109} {:answer/id #uuid "93450f80-7305-5aec-b8ec-a22229ad2662" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{3{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289110} {:answer/id #uuid "6259b2e9-3e7b-59b7-bfb0-173616ef23cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bddc3cf2-3f22-5caf-93ac-23307c7115ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289109} :answer-field/id #uuid "741db9be-5b9b-54e5-9fe9-b7b974d0dd70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2f0b068-41b8-5842-8ef3-240b1ca8e48a" :question/math-academy-id "q-114287" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe, substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{-3x}+2\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x{e}^{-3x}+2\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f437192-3fd7-5be0-8add-e8b38339eea7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{8x}}{8}+\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289114} {:answer/id #uuid "7051331b-9832-5d38-9313-dacb894e97ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{4}+\\frac{5{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289115} {:answer/id #uuid "b48058c2-5346-5519-abbb-5bcf8354e302" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289116} {:answer/id #uuid "a2b92c9b-f60c-56d1-afd4-919813dc0996" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289117} {:answer/id #uuid "7373ec35-03b3-5775-897d-2e1f54523943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{8}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b48058c2-5346-5519-abbb-5bcf8354e302" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289116} :answer-field/id #uuid "86fb0546-a595-54c5-b395-d753ce6ff53f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a8cff6a-f726-5f01-b056-1c73c4cb34b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-114288" :question/problem "$\\int 4x{e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 4x{e}^{8x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=4x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=4 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{8x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{8}{e}^{8x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 4x\\cdot {e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}{e}^{8x}-\\int \\frac{1}{8}{e}^{8x}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4x{e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{8x}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30a0088b-1923-5fdb-ada8-dbb91684be77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2-3x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289121} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c2f046-0e1e-54bb-b647-df1e1bbac18c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x-1){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289122} {:answer/id #uuid "02327162-99a5-5018-a182-2a304b5ce1e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289123} {:answer/id #uuid "1a8148c3-1142-5af7-8bb5-d1aa9d1c6016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2-x){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289124} {:answer/id #uuid "5840cb45-3abb-5479-8451-bbb65798a149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x-1){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02327162-99a5-5018-a182-2a304b5ce1e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289123} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfcb73e0-5c96-58fc-a6e5-c62cb4c5e84c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289120}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "22b47a5c-d440-5039-af24-74694e9daefc" :question/math-academy-id "q-114293" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x-4\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (3x-4)\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =(3x-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{(3x-4){e}^{-3x}}{3}+\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{(3x-4){e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{(3x-3){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C \\\\  & =(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "654b3963-72be-5d2d-ab21-468291cae36b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289128} {:answer/id #uuid "9c08afd9-7502-5e45-bcae-5d34da2f52b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289129} {:answer/id #uuid "d7fb474c-7e53-5437-9a65-388ead62564c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289130} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b781ec-938b-5f02-8e23-aac6bda548c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289131} {:answer/id #uuid "20e24aae-7294-5f43-b360-89d0d52fcba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20e24aae-7294-5f43-b360-89d0d52fcba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289132} :answer-field/id #uuid "097e307a-baf0-562a-a260-70b760dce7bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e39f59c6-1dff-56e6-932b-2ba7bba5a751" :question/math-academy-id "q-114297" :question/problem "$\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c363b1e4-ca51-5471-8e33-ce4fab83915a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289135} {:answer/id #uuid "ceaa5544-28b2-5406-9aba-4a17e48e9d62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289136} {:answer/id #uuid "25bd4a24-6a2d-512f-9a80-78111b9e46c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289137} {:answer/id #uuid "a59e50f6-012a-51fe-aa5a-c0873ac26fa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289138} {:answer/id #uuid "6c69d6d4-44ca-5592-b031-4859ad271a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c69d6d4-44ca-5592-b031-4859ad271a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289139} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c28147d-36e4-5ede-800d-179032583cc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3927a442-7821-55f2-aba3-bde17aab07b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-114311" :question/problem "$\\int (2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x+3\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (2x+3)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(2x+3)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289140 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f55817f1-d0c7-5040-b35e-ec4ee3f947ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289142} {:answer/id #uuid "9282af3b-81a0-582a-84c3-c48741017a33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289143} {:answer/id #uuid "644b3aaf-cefd-5234-8335-739a32ab175c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289144} {:answer/id #uuid "6241a189-3434-5fa7-bd6a-1f84f8396f56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289145} {:answer/id #uuid "fb574e6c-2f2a-5f5c-8b49-3b144168df1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9282af3b-81a0-582a-84c3-c48741017a33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289143} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2ca7314-1853-5a2e-a8a4-327cd176b8ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e9ee642b-9c85-56dd-a07d-2fe51c8fec98" :question/math-academy-id "q-114314" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡x\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={csc}^{2}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ where $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24736613-630b-55f9-819a-105d0c0a9e05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289149} {:answer/id #uuid "a70e6a6f-7ef1-53d0-9f4e-395353be66a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289150} {:answer/id #uuid "64dcb982-2410-5312-a3a8-32b772bb9b83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289151} {:answer/id #uuid "aafc5bd6-10a3-5fce-a049-6753b52ab1be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289152} {:answer/id #uuid "67a7fc43-9fda-544e-84ff-d25caa3092e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aafc5bd6-10a3-5fce-a049-6753b52ab1be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289152} :answer-field/id #uuid "e565e2c1-f70a-54e4-bdf6-b1c175431f0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3972fccf-fd67-52cd-ade5-97cff4fde1d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-114320" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-1}^{0}3x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-2x} & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}3x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}{|}_{-1}^{0}+\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}{|}_{-1}^{0}-\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{-2x}{|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[0{e}^{-2(0)}-(-1){e}^{-2(-1)}]-\\frac{3}{4}[{e}^{-2(0)}-{e}^{-2(-1)}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[0+{e}^{2}]-\\frac{3}{4}[1-{e}^{2}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289154 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33f83f5e-ab39-5c59-a1da-895918f6c799" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{4}+\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289156} {:answer/id #uuid "e8b9c357-a3eb-5d0a-a9ec-b4355d6c9831" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289157} {:answer/id #uuid "ddfe3b31-f7ec-5c69-8ab2-ab63332be930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289158} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b1a02a-d530-5d62-99d9-a63f1e0d8f74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289159} {:answer/id #uuid "b68b56b6-bf5d-5526-851c-1ce7aff442fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{4}-\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5b1a02a-d530-5d62-99d9-a63f1e0d8f74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289159} :answer-field/id #uuid "654d3da2-47f2-5194-a575-68fe6213b525" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4b37af6e-76fe-5074-b739-7927c18f01a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-12560" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int (x+7){e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (x+7){e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+7\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{2x+5}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x+7)\\cdot {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =(x+7)\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+7){e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289161 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ecd12ba-ead6-5c9b-8b19-d74505a582ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289163} {:answer/id #uuid "063f1038-b031-50a8-9960-e1cfd90959d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289164} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b17332-732c-555e-b0f4-f4f78b98b353" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289165} {:answer/id #uuid "48db7a12-5f2d-570a-af53-80aeae1b7bc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289166} {:answer/id #uuid "a3040a83-50d0-52cd-83d6-0701b7b0b560" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4b17332-732c-555e-b0f4-f4f78b98b353" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289165} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca396769-eb6d-53cf-8398-a4cc0df729e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39c1f4f6-a031-555a-af2e-76dd70b7318e" :question/math-academy-id "q-14453" :question/problem "$\\int 6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))+C \\\\  & =6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b33630c-ecb5-56f2-ac14-1b6e8f4d8588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289170} {:answer/id #uuid "d1e0ce0e-76dc-5a7d-997d-67b939ee60fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289171} {:answer/id #uuid "8b16bd54-1ca7-5f2f-b410-221a5b572f89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289172} {:answer/id #uuid "45a33943-b861-59c1-89c3-26eb11f72abd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289173} {:answer/id #uuid "ad468f28-f450-5fa3-868d-b9834bd738d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(1-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b16bd54-1ca7-5f2f-b410-221a5b572f89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289172} :answer-field/id #uuid "f875e6b9-8981-5816-a243-dbaaacb5933a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289169}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0fee3246-3b94-5446-856c-0c95a1862f47" :question/math-academy-id "q-2420" :question/problem "$\\int x{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{5}^{x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={5}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\int \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\int \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\frac{{5}^{x}}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5))^{2}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289175 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa6ddf20-2c4e-5339-9f97-9782ac10c944" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa6ddf20-2c4e-5339-9f97-9782ac10c944" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289177} :answer-field/id #uuid "6660f982-ce9e-5cdb-bd76-ec38a76c647d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "104a55a5-693b-5c53-8ef0-cafe5e29693f" :question/math-academy-id "q-349297" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}9x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=9x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=9 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⇒ & v=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 9x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =9x\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\cdot 9\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}9x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3}-3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot 0-0\\cdot 0)+(-1-1) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47159201-f331-5c83-8ddc-383828eab39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289180} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec45187-f1eb-5762-bc52-0346ef62c508" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2-{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289181} {:answer/id #uuid "79884932-1291-545f-9074-499a42fc8d05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289182} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c8873c-e846-535c-974e-1e7cb0f4edec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-3{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289183} {:answer/id #uuid "e70e8dbd-5827-511d-a205-b64b96acb6b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1+{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47159201-f331-5c83-8ddc-383828eab39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289180} :answer-field/id #uuid "194e6f4a-2d92-5da0-9dac-d53c5bf8c3a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7920756-127c-56a7-b85e-2c3d28bb75c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-49660" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-2}^{0}x{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-x} & ⇒ & v=-{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (-{e}^{-x})-\\int (-{e}^{-x})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}x{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-x{e}^{-x}{|}_{-2}^{0}+{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x{e}^{-x}{|}_{-2}^{0}-{e}^{-x}{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =[-0{e}^{-0}-2{e}^{2}]-[{e}^{0}-{e}^{2}] \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2}-1+{e}^{2} \\\\  & =-1-{e}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289185 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66ed67ab-3b6d-5376-99af-1521eea874b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289187} {:answer/id #uuid "f480ed02-4683-599b-9ea8-e0ed4fd0efd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289188} {:answer/id #uuid "d7f549d5-ec1b-5f55-8351-0b279065d82f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289189} {:answer/id #uuid "2c615c85-2408-520b-93c5-a68a79e4cd64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289190} {:answer/id #uuid "281be117-ac80-5d7e-84e8-b14e444e95fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7f549d5-ec1b-5f55-8351-0b279065d82f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289189} :answer-field/id #uuid "dce6354e-cb58-579c-8cec-f01d83452d90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289186}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30d59cec-59a4-58ed-913f-20fcfb228f0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-49669" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into  the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={-\\frac{2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}|}_{0}^{\\pi /6}+\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={-\\frac{2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}|}_{0}^{\\pi /6}+{\\frac{2}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}[\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & +\\frac{2}{9}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}[0-0]+\\frac{2}{9}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2202011-f89c-5347-ba9b-ecf730a87cb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289194} {:answer/id #uuid "fddf3212-9334-5ea0-af72-69b858fd25a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289195} {:answer/id #uuid "819ecb8d-76ca-5088-89ba-70c3ffc074f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289196} {:answer/id #uuid "734b65ea-919d-5772-b4e4-6607d840ef8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289197} {:answer/id #uuid "9b13811f-4a58-54c3-8790-3494d297b97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b13811f-4a58-54c3-8790-3494d297b97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289198} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffc1d0ca-a504-534b-b970-16556e359de2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "defa81e9-682b-527a-b8b7-4cbfb3842b1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49674" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & ⇒ & v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}-{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x){|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})]+\\frac{1}{4}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}]+\\frac{1}{4}[0-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[0]+0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289199 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "198c8f4c-56f0-5207-af5e-9ea835359917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289201} {:answer/id #uuid "7d30a13c-f8c3-5850-8b27-454978932aa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{10}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289202} {:answer/id #uuid "76c5e5f4-76f8-5470-82b6-cc171144b920" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289203} {:answer/id #uuid "1b8c7ce4-cac6-509c-b60c-8658bc94214a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289204} {:answer/id #uuid "b53d9767-eb38-5f96-a8b7-c6784af37754" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{10}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "198c8f4c-56f0-5207-af5e-9ea835359917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289201} :answer-field/id #uuid "75d982fc-1d07-5ed6-830c-726192ed99e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c21d0dc3-2df8-5b24-86c4-408d7b44edd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-74090" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=10x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=10 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 10x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10x\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))\\cdot 10\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-10\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
